      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's very important to consult with a pediatrician for proper medical advice, especially with an 18-month-old infant. Generally speaking, the recommended dosage of infant acetaminophen (Tylenol) is around 15 milligrams per kilogram of body weight, aside from a food-related snack to avoid stomach upset. For your 11 kg baby, this would be approximately 165 mg of acetaminophen (15 mg/kg x 11 kg). This dosage falls close to the 160mg per 5mL liquid formulation, but a healthcare professional should confirm this for his safety. Do not administer medication without proper guidance from a doctor or pharmacist.",
